/F1 11 Tf
50 780 Td
14 TL
/F1 18 Tf
(Database and Deployment Workflow) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(Database Tables) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
(Users: stores user profile, email, password hash, and created date.) Tj
T*
(Categories: stores user-specific income and expense categories.) Tj
T*
(Transactions: stores category relationship, amount, type, date, description,) Tj
T*
(and recurring status.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(Relationships) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
(- One user has many categories.) Tj
T*
(- One user has many transactions.) Tj
T*
(- One category has many transactions.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(Local Run Workflow) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
(1. Start backend with: mvn spring-boot:run) Tj
T*
(2. Backend runs at: http://localhost:8080) Tj
T*
(3. Start frontend with: npm run dev) Tj
T*
(4. Frontend runs at: http://localhost:5173) Tj
T*
(5. Login using demo credentials or create a new account.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(Deployment Workflow) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
(1. Build backend using: mvn clean package) Tj
T*
(2. Build frontend using: npm run build) Tj
T*
(3. Host backend JAR on a server with Java installed.) Tj
T*
(4. Host frontend dist folder on a static server.) Tj
T*
(5. Configure frontend API URL for the deployed backend.) Tj
T*
(6. Replace H2 with MySQL, PostgreSQL, or SQL Server for production use.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
